{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol","id":236235,"title":"Frenzy vs Idol","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-20T23:58:20-07:00","id":236235,"title":"Frenzy vs Idol","content":"I don't know how to word my question! A vampire lost in a killing frenzy... A vampire with idol active... Does vamp A get an auto pass on the rolls to attack vamp B or would the frenzy be subdued? Would the frenzy be pushed to another available target? Could they even frenzy with intent to kill if idol was active?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T03:56:44-07:00","id":236317,"title":"","content":"Depends on the circumstances really. If the vampire with Idol active Awed or Charmed the frenzying vampire first, they 'might' be able to redirect it, presuming they aren't the direct cause. If the frenzying vampire wasn't subjected to Awe or charmed by the vampire using Idol first or he turns on Idol in hopes of redirecting it, it's an auto fail.<br /> <br /> Yes you can enter frenzy with Idol active. There are currently no disciplines that prohibit you from entering frenzy. Only a Touchstone can talk a vampire out of frenzy and it's not instantaneous. Frenzy is one of the reasons why most vampire society has a social contract about NOT violating each other at will with disciplines because the vampire you violated may decide to reciprocate on you by Riding the Wave with a splintered Louisville Slugger in their hands. Frenzy is useful for blunting or ending some types of mind or emotion control but since you normally have to kill or perform massive property damage before dropping out of frenzy it will likely erode your Humanity fairly quickly and or/make the local authorities consider your existence a liability to society they can ill-afford.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:01:20-07:00","id":236333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol#post236235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the frenzy be pushed to another available target?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly it. Check out the last paragraph that starts on pg. 104. You can use Disciplines to shift the focus of a vampire's Frenzy, but you can't shut it down. Doesn't matter if the power was active pre-Frenzy, or it's popped off after a vamp flips her lid.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:28:52-07:00","id":236362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=236333#post236333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly it. Check out the last paragraph that starts on pg. 104. You can use Disciplines to shift the focus of a vampire's Frenzy, but you can't shut it down. Doesn't matter if the power was active pre-Frenzy, or it's popped off after a vamp flips her lid.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly what I was thinking. Idol prevents people/vampires from even wanting to harm you. You have to make a roll to do anything that could harm the vampire, so if the 1 vampire wanted to throw themselves into a frenzy with the sole purpose of harming the vampire wouldn't that go against Idol. If I understand, idol is reflexive, anyone's turn, and frenzy is instant, your turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:38:26-07:00","id":236384,"title":"","content":"Resisting frenzy is reflexive (1st paragraph pg 104) in response to something that would trigger a frenzy. You can enter frenzy outside your turn and it doesn't take any sort of action unless you're riding the wave.<br /> <br /> Idol is reflexive, but remember that it modifies Awe and Awe is an instant action. If Awe was already active then that sequence of events works. The vampire frenzies and before she can attack the Prince cranks up Idol reflexively to shift the vampire's target to some other hapless wretch nearby. If the Prince didn't already have Awe up he may have to endure a turn of frenzied savagery before he can fire up his Majesty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:53:37-07:00","id":236392,"title":"","content":"I am talking about the kind of frenzy you can put yourself into, is that riding the wave? The one you do yourself, not because something caused it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T05:57:08-07:00","id":236395,"title":"","content":"I'd say Idol would prevent you from consciously triggering a Frenzy in yourself. You're not stopping the Frenzy, you're stopping the thought process and actions that would lead to a voluntary Frenzy ala Riding the Wave being triggered. With a provoked, natural frenzy you are, of course, shit out of luck.<br /> <br /> Also, the rules on the reflexiveness of Idol are confusing. The discipline says you -can- wait for Awe to be dropped first, or you can simply activate Idol immediately (activating Awe with it automatically). That sounds like Idol potentially makes Awe reflexive.<br /> <br /> To play devil's advocate against ourselves for a moment, Frenzy says that attempts to coerce the beast into behaviour contrary to her desires fail, but is that really what's going on here? You're not making the vampire do anything, you're only keeping them at bay. If the frenzied vampire's desire was to &quot;tear you a new one&quot;, he or she could still be struggling against Idol every turn, trying to get at you. They're still doing exactly what their Beast wants them to do. Putting a leash on something or putting a road block in their way is making the successful execution of their desires harder, sure, but it's not coercing them into a new behaviour at all. (In a way, it's no different from having defense or armour so high that you can't be harmed by the other vampire. You're not changing their behaviour, but mitigating their chance of success.)The example given is about Dominate directly giving orders to someone, which is a bit different than Majesty's &quot;do not fuck me up&quot; aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-21-2014, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:19:54-07:00","id":236409,"title":"","content":"Right, Vitalis, that's riding the wave. I agree with Unahim that if you're currently affected by Idol you would not be able to ride the wave unless the vampire using Idol gave you permission to go sick house on someone, or you successfully challenge the power with the reflexive Resolve + Blood Potency - user's Majesty dots.<br /> <br /> If you succeed at that you can then begin trying to ride the wave. Remember that you have to repeat the roll for each individual action you want to take that violates the Idol, so unless you hammer your first riding the wave check with an exceptional success it becomes a very tricky proposition. I would rule that if you begin riding the wave, then fail one of the Idol rolls you are treated as failing to ride the wave and immediately enter frenzy (remember that it counts as a dramatic failure on a resist frenzy roll). You'd still be subject to the active Idol power and can try to contest it to attack the user as normal, but if you fail you'll be redirected to another target.<br /> <br /> Unahim: That part in Idol is just explaining that you don't have to activate it when you activate Awe. You can have Awe up on its own, then you can fire up Idol later to push your Awe into overdrive. Or you can pay the cost of Idol immediately when you activate Awe and get all the effects at once. It's not saying you can activate Awe as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> Using Idol to force a frenzied vampire to back down and cower is most certainly trying to coerce the Beast into behavior contrary to her desires. The Beast wants to rip that fucker's throat out and bathe in his blood. Idol says, &quot;Sit, doggy.&quot; You can't make the frenzied vamp back down, but you can shift her away from you, assuming she failed her roll to act against the Idol. The Dominate example was just that, an example, not an exhaustive list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:23:01-07:00","id":236411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=236395#post236395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the rules on the reflexiveness of Idol are confusing. The discipline says you -can- wait for Awe to be dropped first, or you can simply activate Idol immediately (activating Awe with it automatically). That sounds like Idol potentially makes Awe reflexive</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked once long ago about this, I believe Rose! said it does both in one reflexive action... I suppose I should start digging for that thread.... Lol!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-21-2014, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:24:07-07:00","id":236412,"title":"","content":"Ooo. I'd be very interested to see that if you can find it.<br /> <br /> Ah, I found where you were talking about whether or not you have to pay the cost of Idol when you activate it along with Awe. It's still pretty clear that it doesn't change the activation action of Awe (instant). Rose and PenDragon suggested that when you have Idol, you should think of it as changing the way Awe works to Cost: None, or 2 Vitae and 1 Willpower. Nothing about the activation time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 08-21-2014, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:40:08-07:00","id":236420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=236411#post236411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked once long ago about this, I believe toes said it does both in one reflexive action... I suppose I should start digging for that thread.... Lol!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thread I was thinking of as well, but we might both be mistaken. Anyway, Smarmy, I did say I was playing Devil's Advocate: I wouldn't personally rule that way in my games. But it's very easy to see someone arguing for Idol being basically invisible bonds holding you back. I would say the &quot;Sit, doggy.&quot; part is only relating to those you've charmed who are now Enthralled.<br /> <br /> Actually, I've checked the thread now as well (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/89202-discipline-majesty-idol\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-majesty-idol</a>), and I'm still not convinced you can't reflexively activate Idol and Awe. PenDragon says that when Awe isn't in effect, it and Idol activate simultaneously. He doesn't say that this can only happen on your turn.<br /> <br /> Then Rose talks about accounting for the time between two reflexive actions, as if she thinks Awe is also reflexive. The obvious conclusion being that she thinks Idol should be able to be activated reflexively even when Awe isn't on. I could be wrong and misreading her, of course, but if I am then why bring that second reflexive action in there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 08-21-2014, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:44:02-07:00","id":236423,"title":"","content":"Yeah yeah, I was just running the counterpoint to your advocacy. I wouldn't rule it as invisible bonds either, but emotional deflection if you fail the challenge roll. The Beast just shifts away from whatever the hell THAT thing is (the Idol user) and goes after something it can more easily annihilate.<br /> <br /> This is good discussion, and I appreciate a good Devil's Advocate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T06:56:35-07:00","id":236429,"title":"","content":"Ah! you beat me to it! Since Idol is reflexive, you can do it whenever and activate both, That's how we have been using it!.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-21-2014, 09:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:01:47-07:00","id":236431,"title":"","content":"That's definitely not what that thread was saying, but there's nothing wrong with your group playing it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:03:05-07:00","id":236432,"title":"","content":"This is helpful stuff and I thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:22:56-07:00","id":236442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/89202-discipline-majesty-idol?p=89291#post89291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You must always pay the price.<br /> <br /> If Awe was already active, Idols effects kick in on top of it. If Awe isn't active, it and Idol activate simultaneously. It's better not to think of them as two separate powers though, Idol is a natural extension of Awe. Awe's cost basically becomes (Cost: None or 2 Vitae &amp; 1 Willpower)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/89202-discipline-majesty-idol?p=89759#post89759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PenDragon is right. The text, which may be slightly unclear, just means that Awe doesn't have to be activated before paying the cost and activating Idol. That's to prevent players from thinking they need to account for timing between two reflexive actions, which can, by the rules, happen effectively at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought it is what the thread said... Idol is a relexive action ^ they Both say it happens at the same time... Perhaps I am mistaken on how reflexive works? I thought you can do it outside &quot;your turn&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:30:50-07:00","id":236470,"title":"","content":"They are not talking about the action per se, they're talking about the cost.<br /> <br /> Awe's action is Instant. PenDragon is saying to think of Idol less as a separate power, and more as a new option added to Awe. It's still an instant action to activate Awe, but now you can choose to pay the higher cost to boost its power. That cost is paid as a reflexive action either immediately when you activate Awe (still an Instant action) or at any later time while Awe is running (in this case it can be done at any time, even outside your own turn since paying the Idol cost is a reflexive action).<br /> <br /> Awe's action is always instant. Boosting Awe with Idol is reflexive, but need not be done at the same time as you spend your instant action to activate Awe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:36:38-07:00","id":236472,"title":"","content":"<i>if Awe isn't active, it and Idol activate simultaneously<br /> <br /> just means that Awe doesn't have to be activated before paying the cost and activating Idol.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ok. I am not trying to be a butt here. I am just trying to understand. We are clearly interpreting this very differently. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 08-21-2014, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-21T07:39:08-07:00","id":236474,"title":"","content":"Yes. They activate simultaneously. With an instant action to turn on Awe, and a reflexive action to simultaneously activate Idol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:34:22-07:00","id":237281,"title":"","content":"I actually don't agree, Smarmy. PenDragon never stipulates you can only do it on your turn, something that would have been appreciated if it remained an instant action. Rose talks about the time between two reflexive actions. Which two? Awe and Idol, naturally. Maybe she made a mistake and thought Awe was always reflexive, but in that case I would still lean towards it being reflexive, as it is obviously her intention for the combination of the two to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:48:05-07:00","id":237286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=237281#post237281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually don't agree, Smarmy. PenDragon never stipulates you can only do it on your turn, something that would have been appreciated if it remained an instant action. Rose talks about the time between two reflexive actions. Which two? Awe and Idol, naturally. Maybe she made a mistake and thought Awe was always reflexive, but in that case I would still lean towards it being reflexive, as it is obviously her intention for the combination of the two to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a mistake. Awe changed between reflexive and instant during development, and I mis-posted. Sorry about that.<br /> <br /> Idol can be activated functionally simultaneously with Awe, but you still have to spend the instant action somewhere in there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:51:13-07:00","id":237290,"title":"","content":"Idol enhances Awe, therefore it cannot be used unless Awe is in effect. However, it doesn't have to be activated simultaneously with Awe. A Vampire could, if they want, activate Awe (and Instant Action) and simultaneously activate Idol (Reflexive), or activate Awe then wait for a while and turn on Idol several turns later (Before people ask: Yes, that means he can turn on Idol in the middle of someone else's action). What he can't do is go from being his average, non-majestic self, straight to being the singular locus of adoration, without first taking an action to turn on Awe.<br /> <br /> Hopefully that clears things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T14:21:35-07:00","id":237357,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the clarification, Rose and PenDragon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T20:25:08-07:00","id":237657,"title":"","content":"Well, word of god and all that. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T09:43:18-08:00","id":1054809,"title":"","content":"Sorry for digging up the old topic, but what about a situation when a vampire A has eternal frenzy coil to be already in frenzy (ride the wave) and wants to kill vampire B, who activates Idol discipline? Is it auto fail? Does the vampire A gets a BP bonus to the roll to resist it or what? IMHO it is a BP bonus, but I'm not sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:12:29-08:00","id":1054823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1054809#post1054809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for digging up the old topic, but what about a situation when a vampire A has eternal frenzy coil to be already in frenzy (ride the wave) and wants to kill vampire B, who activates Idol discipline? Is it auto fail? Does the vampire A gets a BP bonus to the roll to resist it or what? IMHO it is a BP bonus, but I'm not sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oohh Old stuff! <br /> <br /> Bob is in a riding the wave in a kill frenzy and Dave does not want to be killed so he pops Idol. Bob will still need to roll Resolve + BP \u2013 5 to attack Dave, because Dave is just the most amazing thing in the world and surely killing something else instead would be better than hurting Dave or hurting his feelings. They would have to roll that every turn that they wanted to hurt Dave.<br /> <br /> However my group we play with if you fail once, you have just chickened out and the desire to harm dissipates. Unless Dave does something quite awful to provoke something, like perhaps kill your best friend. It's not like a bubble where you are just prevented from touching them and you're still full of hate and rage... It messes with your emotions and desires shift. You dont even want to hurt them anymore. ( and that includes hurting their feelings. &quot;cant even crack a joke&quot; )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:20:37-08:00","id":1054828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1054823#post1054823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oohh Old stuff!<br /> <br /> Bob is in a riding the wave in a kill frenzy and Dave does not want to be killed so he pops Idol. Bob will still need to roll Resolve + BP \u2013 5 to attack Dave, because Dave is just the most amazing thing in the world and surely killing something else instead would be better than hurting Dave or hurting his feelings. They would have to roll that every turn that they wanted to hurt Dave.<br /> <br /> However my group we play with if you fail once, you have just chickened out and the desire to harm dissipates. Unless Dave does something quite awful to provoke something, like perhaps kill your best friend. It's not like a bubble where you are just prevented from touching them and you're still full of hate and rage... It messes with your emotions and desires shift. You dont even want to hurt them anymore. ( and that includes hurting their feelings. &quot;cant even crack a joke&quot; )</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, but doesn't the frenzy somehow affect the resistance roll: resistance+BP-5? I guess it's more difficult to affect a frenzied vampire with Majesty.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (...) Add her Blood Potency dots to any Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina rolls or resistances </div> </div> </div>isn't it resolve+BP+BP-5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-25-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:28:10-08:00","id":1054832,"title":"","content":"If the frenzy was turned on with the goal set before coming in proximity of the Idol user who tries to turn it on, frenzy wins. If he tries to turn on frenzy after coming into proximity of the Idol user who has Idol on already, he has to make the roll first to overcome Idol if he wants to target the Idol user for violence.<br /> <br /> For simplicity sake, I'd probably just have both characters to do a clash of wills to see who's effect prevails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T10:32:47-08:00","id":1054841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1054832#post1054832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the frenzy was turned on with the goal set before coming in proximity of the Idol user who tries to turn it on, frenzy wins. If he tries to turn on frenzy after coming into proximity of the Idol user who has Idol on already, he has to make the roll first to overcome Idol if he wants to target the Idol user for violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks ok, what about the bonus to the roll? Does it apply?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1054832#post1054832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For simplicity sake, I'd probably just have both characters to do a clash of wills to see who's effect prevails.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the simplicity rule looks kinda fishy, because the Coil of The Wyrm isn't a discipline.<br /> <br /> EUREKA:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Add her Blood Potency dots to any Strength, Dexterity, or Stamina rolls or resistances</i> </div> </div> </div>**** Damn resistances are strength+brawl-strength rolls or all composure, resolve, stamina rolls to resist something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":".  EUREKA 02-25-2017, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:17:54-08:00","id":1054877,"title":"","content":"Bonus to what roll? Ride the Wave, yes. To overcome Idol, that's ST fiat. <br /> <br /> Being a discipline versus a mystery is why I would roll a Clash of Wills. Whenever the mechanics of a power come into direct conflict with another power and there's no clear delineation of which trumps the other is when you would roll a clash of wills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:22:28-08:00","id":1054882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1054877#post1054877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bonus to what roll? Ride the Wave, yes. To overcome Idol, that's ST fiat.<br /> <br /> Being a discipline versus a mystery is why I would roll a Clash of Wills. Whenever the mechanics of a power come into direct conflict with another power and there's no clear delineation of which trumps the other is when you would roll a clash of wills.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that the frenzy BP bonus also applies to all resistance attribute rolls, but now I have a feeling the intent was to rolls such as strength+brawl-strength","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12872,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","user":"Edgar McAlister","date":". 02-25-2017, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:43:34-08:00","id":1054893,"title":"","content":"You add your mystery rating to the BP enhancing effects you gain while in frenzy. It's up to the ST if overcoming Idol counts as a resist check. (I say it is personally.) <br /> I think the power was meant to enhance resist checks against powers that deduct a target's Stamina from the dice pool or where your resist check consists of Resistance Attribute + BP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T11:43:57-08:00","id":1054894,"title":"","content":"*rises from torpor*<br /> <br /> Huh? Oh! Hey guys. <br /> <br /> Edgar: The +BP stuff definitely only applies to physical attribute rolls/resistance. <br /> <br /> Check out the second-to-last paragraph on pg 104. &quot;If a character tries to coerce her to behavior contrary to the Beast's desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails. They can, however, divert the Beast's attention to another, similar target.&quot; <br /> <br /> The character invoking Idol can't stop the frenzy entirely, but it will convince the frenzied vampire to go after a different target (assuming it fails to overcome Idol using the normal system).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T17:10:36-08:00","id":1055001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1054894#post1054894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*rises from torpor*<br /> <br /> Huh? Oh! Hey guys.<br /> <br /> Edgar: The +BP stuff definitely only applies to physical attribute rolls/resistance.<br /> <br /> Check out the second-to-last paragraph on pg 104. &quot;If a character tries to coerce her to behavior contrary to the Beast's desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines, the effort fails. They can, however, divert the Beast's attention to another, similar target.&quot;<br /> <br /> The character invoking Idol can't stop the frenzy entirely, but it will convince the frenzied vampire to go after a different target (assuming it fails to overcome Idol using the normal system).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you for the explanation, so I guess in rare occasions Idol might not work when there are no other targets, but in most cases it works, but the frenzy doesn't stop, since the target of frenzy is changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12872-edgar-mcalister","name":"Edgar McAlister","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-25T18:02:29-08:00","id":1055015,"title":"","content":"The Idol tactic won't work on someone who has mastered the Coils of the Wyrm if they already selected their target using Ride the Wave. Trying to direct frenzy to someone else would auto fail since it runs contrary to the Beast's desire. The character can also simply redirect back to their original target cost free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:56:13-08:00","id":1056209,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Edgar McAlister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1055001#post1055001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, thank you for the explanation, so I guess in rare occasions Idol might not work when there are no other targets, but in most cases it works, but the frenzy doesn't stop, since the target of frenzy is changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI would think there are always other targets. Just that target might be across the street or down the hall, or outside.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/236235-frenzy-vs-idol?p=1055015#post1055015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Idol tactic won't work on someone who has mastered the Coils of the Wyrm if they already selected their target using Ride the Wave. Trying to direct frenzy to someone else would auto fail since it runs contrary to the Beast's desire. The character can also simply redirect back to their original target cost free.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they would have to roll to redirect it back to the original target. Because if you failed the person who frenzied, could choose to come out of the frenzy. Maybe you chicken out and decide it's a bad idea...<br /> <br /> <i>He has no more control over his actions than he would<br /> in an involuntary frenzy (p. 103), and all rolls to escape frenzy<br /> before the stated objective is met are made at a \u20132 die penalty.</i><br /> <u><b><i>When the original goal is no longer pressing or possible, the<br /> frenzy ends</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or mastered: </b></u><br /> <br /> <i>Fortunately, he may now<br /> retain his frenzy past the end of the scene, riding the wave from<br /> impulse to impulse until he is destroyed, or sleep takes him.</i><br /> <u><b><i>(He may also choose to leave frenzy at the end of any scene.)</i></b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Small issue, Redirecting doesn't &quot;Autofail&quot; Trying to coerce the vampire against the beasts will does. Like Dominating them to tell them to hug their friend when they are in a death frenzy, Persuading them not to feed on you with a manipulation roll would also autofail. If you see the text in frenzy it says that you CAN redirect them. If they are in a kill frenzy you have them kill someone else, the beasts wants to kill and that's not against the beast's desires. <br /> <br /> <i>\u200bIf a character tries to coerce her to behavior contrary to the<br /> Beast\u2019s desires, either via Social actions or through Disciplines,<br /> the effort fails. <u><b>They can, however, divert the Beast\u2019s attention<br /> to another, similar target.</b></u> For example, if Veronica falls to<br /> her Beast due to hunger and leaps at Elspeth, Elspeth might<br /> Dominate her to attack Dominic instead</i><br /> <br /> <br /> All text in <i>Italics </i>is copied and pasted directly from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 02-28-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}